{
    "background_story": "Estella was a free-spirited artist who spent her youth traveling the world, soaking up inspiration from diverse cultures. In her mid-twenties, she stumbled upon a traditional Korean instrument, the gayageum, while exploring a market in Seoul. Entranced by its unique sound, Estella dedicated herself to mastering the instrument. She spent years studying under the guidance of a renowned Korean musician, eventually earning the title of 'jong,' or master musician. Estella's music became a fusion of traditional Korean sounds with modern, global influences. Her soulful performances captivated audiences worldwide, earning her a reputation as a true innovator in the world music scene. Estella's journey was a testament to the power of cross-cultural exchange and the beauty of traditional arts.",
